Usage:  key child DERIVATION-PATH

  Derive child keys from a parent public/private key

Available options:
  -h,--help                Show this help text
  DERIVATION-PATH          Slash-separated derivation path.
                           Hardened indexes are marked with a 'H'
                           or a single quote (e.g.
                           1852H/1815H/0H/0 or
                           m/1852'/1815'/0'/2/0).

The parent key is read from stdin. Hardened indexes can be written with the legacy 'H' suffix or the standard single-quote (') suffix. An optional 'm/' prefix denotes absolute derivation from the master key.
